.IX Title "Lucy::Analysis::SnowballStopFilter 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Analysis::SnowballStopFilter 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Analysis::SnowballStopFilter \- Suppress a “stoplist” of common words.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 6
\&    my $stopfilter = Lucy::Analysis::SnowballStopFilter\->new(
\&        language => \*(Aqfr\*(Aq,
\&    );
\&    my $polyanalyzer = Lucy::Analysis::PolyAnalyzer\->new(
\&        analyzers => [ $tokenizer, $normalizer, $stopfilter, $stemmer ],
\&    );
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
A “stoplist” is collection of “stopwords”: words which are common enough to
be of little value when determining search results.  For example, so many
documents in English contain “the”, “if”, and “maybe” that it may improve
both performance and relevance to block them.
.PP
Before filtering stopwords:
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    ("i", "am", "the", "walrus")
.Ve
.PP
After filtering stopwords:
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    ("walrus")
.Ve
.PP
SnowballStopFilter provides default stoplists for several languages,
courtesy of the Snowball project <http://snowball.tartarus.org>, or you may
supply your own.
.PP
.Vb 10
\&    |\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-|
\&    | ISO CODE | LANGUAGE   |
\&    |\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-|
\&    | da       | Danish     |
\&    | de       | German     |
\&    | en       | English    |
\&    | es       | Spanish    |
\&    | fi       | Finnish    |
\&    | fr       | French     |
\&    | hu       | Hungarian  |
\&    | it       | Italian    |
\&    | nl       | Dutch      |
\&    | no       | Norwegian  |
\&    | pt       | Portuguese |
\&    | sv       | Swedish    |
\&    | ru       | Russian    |
\&    |\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-|
.Ve
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 3
\&    my $stopfilter = Lucy::Analysis::SnowballStopFilter\->new(
\&        language => \*(Aqde\*(Aq,
\&    );
\&    
\&    # or...
\&    my $stopfilter = Lucy::Analysis::SnowballStopFilter\->new(
\&        stoplist => \e%stoplist,
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Create a new SnowballStopFilter.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBstoplist\fR \- A hash with stopwords as the keys.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBlanguage\fR \- The ISO code for a supported language.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS transform
.IX Subsection "transform"
.Vb 1
\&    my $inversion = $snowball_stop_filter\->transform($inversion);
.Ve
.PP
Take a single Inversion as input
and returns an Inversion, either the same one (presumably transformed
in some way), or a new one.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBinversion\fR \- An inversion.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Lucy::Analysis::SnowballStopFilter isa Lucy::Analysis::Analyzer isa Clownfish::Obj.
